{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 250,
    "dDurationMs": 4311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We take navigation for granted these days\n- GPS receivers guide airplanes, cars, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4561,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even cell phones!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5561,
    "dDurationMs": 4459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But did you know that the Global Positioning\nSystem is basically a big clock in space?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10020,
    "dDurationMs": 3699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are thirty GPS satellites in orbit,\nand they just broadcast where they are and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13719,
    "dDurationMs": 1181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what time it is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14900,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All your phone GPS has to do is receive signals\nfrom four satellites and it can triangulate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19460,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its location in the four dimensions in which\nwe live – three space and one time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24240,
    "dDurationMs": 1790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But actually it's not that simple!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26030,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In order for navigation to work, the satellites\ncarry atomic clocks accurate to the nanosecond"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30550,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– otherwise your GPS receiver might tell\nyou you're halfway across town when you're"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34390,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still in the driveway."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35840,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And special relativity tells us that moving\nclocks run slow, while general relativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39960,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tells us that clocks run faster higher in\na gravitational field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43470,
    "dDurationMs": 4659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These effects don't quite cancel – general\nrelativity wins out and time indeed runs faster"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48129,
    "dDurationMs": 1881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up in orbit with the satellites!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50010,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But some of the engineers working on the first\nGPS satellite couldn't bring themselves to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53860,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "believe that their clock would actually run\nfast just from being higher up, so they sent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57730,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it up uncorrected!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59090,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Within minutes it was off by enough to impair\nGPS navigation, and by the end of the day,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63350,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "GPS receivers would have been wrong by tens\nof kilometers!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66330,
    "dDurationMs": 4079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Needless to say, the engineers turned the\ncorrection back on, and these days they trust"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70409,
    "dDurationMs": 1111,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "general relativity!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71520,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, and one last thing - GPS is also a nuclear\nweapons detector: there are always at least"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76470,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "four GPS satellites visible from any point\non earth, and because of this, any nuclear"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80930,
    "dDurationMs": 4049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "detonation will be seen by enough satellites\nto pinpoint exactly where and when it took"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84979,
    "dDurationMs": 320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "place."
    } ]
  } ]
}
